
== 1 — a grapheme is not a byte and not a code point ==
Zoe with an accent: 0 1 2 4
a family emoji: 0 25
a flag, which this renderer splits: 0 4 8
an Arabic word: 0 2 4 6 8 10

== 2 — the caret moves by grapheme, never into one ==
text is 27 bytes
caret stops moving right: 0 1 26 27 27
and coming back: 27 26 1 0 0

== 3 — a delete removes a whole grapheme ==
after one backspace over the emoji: 2 bytes
what is left: "ab"

== 4 — a selection covers whole graphemes ==
a double-click selects 0..5
which is "café"

== 4b — and a word moves by word, not by character ==
one word right lands at 5
two words right lands at 14

== 5 — a secure field holds text and shows none of it ==
it holds 7 bytes
what it draws: "•••••••"
the two are different: true
